  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "RDMA4-P1-001",
      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "All-ten capitalization unknown makes the positive quota and admission structurally unreachable",
      "affectedArtifacts": [
        "docs/AI_MAPPING_V4_PREREGISTRATION.md",
        "docs/AI_MAPPING_V4_READJUDICATION_PREREGISTRATION_V4.md",
        "pilot/evaluation/v4/readjudication-instructions-v4.md",
        "pilot/evaluation/v4/readjudication-schema-v4.json",
        "pilot/evaluation/v4/readjudication-protocol-seal-v4.json"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        "The v4 schema correctly forces usage.capitalization=unknown in every completed case.",
        "The original and v4 gold rules permit a positive only when every usage axis is match, source-only-preservable, or not-applicable and the usage mismatch is empty.",
        "Unknown is excluded from that set and deterministically creates USAGE_CAPITALIZATION_UNKNOWN, so the maximum possible positive count is 0 while admission requires at least 4 positives."
      ],
      "impact": "No schema-valid C/D adjudication pair can ever reach admission GO, even with perfect ten-case unanimity and ideal semantic and example judgments. Running C/D would consume a blind packet for a foreknown zero-positive result. The design also conflates held-out semantic/example equivalence gold with publication-time usage-metadata completeness: missing capitalization metadata vetoes the evaluation label itself rather than remaining a separate approval or completeness dimension.",
      "requiredDisposition": "Keep v4 blank forms and execution prohibited. Preserve v4 unchanged and preregister a new independently audited contract that separates equivalence gold from publication approval or usage-completeness vetoes, or otherwise uses a fresh packet and criteria whose positive and negative quotas are demonstrably satisfiable without post-result relaxation."
    }
  ],
